This browser application's source is supplied under GPL-2.0-only to retain the
terms of that incorporated table. Source is in src/; reproducible build inputs
are package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, and scripts/.

The USB protocol implementation was carried from this project's experimentally
validated JavaScript path. RGB lookup tables remain identity values. SANE's RGB
calibration tables and C backend are not bundled. TypeScript and WebUSB type
declarations are development dependencies. Automatic upright text uses local
Tesseract.js 7.0.0 and tesseract.js-core 7.0.0 (Apache-2.0), and OSD trained data
from @tesseract.js-data/osd 1.0.0, legacy 4.0.0 data. The data package metadata
uses MIT; the upstream tessdata model is Apache-2.0. Corresponding license texts
and bundled dependency notices are in dist/vendor/ocr/licenses/. Asset hashes
and exact versions are in dist/vendor/ocr/manifest.json. Sources:
https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js
https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js-core
https://github.com/naptha/tessdata
https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tesseract.js-data/osd

The app does not change these third-party license terms. All assets are served
locally from the static site; there is no CDN fallback, scanner service or image
upload endpoint. OCR is optional and initialized only when requested.

Local ICC correction uses lcms-wasm 1.0.5 (MIT), incorporating LittleCMS 2.16
(MIT), and raw JPEG decoding uses jpeg-js 0.4.4 (BSD-3-Clause). License texts,
asset hashes and sRGB destination-profile provenance are in dist/vendor/color/.
The sRGB destination profile is generated by LittleCMS; it does not describe
this scanner. ICC fitting and validation code is in src/color/. Proprietary Epson
resources are inspected locally for research but are not bundled as runtime
calibration assets. esbuild is a build dependency for the JPEG decoder bundle.
